  > > > > > As part of our introduction round\, I’d please ask each partn
 er to prepare a short (5-8 minute or so) presentation on their instituti
 on\, teaching and research areas. I’d also like to ask each of you to pr
 epare an informal “hypothesis" relating to the project (i.e. from your k
 nowledge and experience\, what problems do you think our target group fa
 ce\, what do you think are their relevant needs\, how do you think these
  needs can be met\, what challenges do you think are faced in implementi
 ng this kind of learning\, etc). This should provide us an interesting s
 tarting point for discussions and help us get to know each others’ ideas
  and expectations.\n\n> > > > > > > > > > > > > > > > \n\n> > > > > > > 
 > > > > > > > > One of my priorities for this meeting is that we all go 
 away with a vision for what the project will create\, to have a really c
 lear idea of what we are working towards. For this\, I would please like
  to ask Jose and Ana (UTAD) in particular to prepare a short presentatio
 n about summer school possibilities at the university (experiences so fa
 r of running summer schools\, what UTAD can offer\, etc.).\n\n> > > > > 
 > > > > > > > > > > > \n\n> > > > > > > > > > > > > > > I am very excite
