BEGIN:VEVENT
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20230711T041303Z
DESCRIPTION:Dear all\,\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCall for speakers now open! \n\nnT
 he landscape of ESP in tertiary education is constantly evolving. While 
 the importance of English remains undiminished\, the challenges (and exp
 ectations) facing both students and instructors are changing.\n\n\n\n\n\
 n\n\nAsexpanding number of degree programs prepare students for careers 
 in ever-more specific fields\, the expectations around English competenc
 y are also becoming more specific\, along with the approaches instructor
 s use to meet those needs. Yet\, the essential goal of any ESP course re
 mains the same: to increase the ability and confidence of the student wh
 en using English.  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWith our theme of “Common Ground in E
 SP” for the 202ition of the UAS LIC\, we hope that the diverse group of 
 ESP instructors working in and around Austria will explore what ESP mean
 s to them\, and how their experiences can be related to the field more g
 enerally. This means both offering insight into their specific teaching 
 context and highlighting common threads and unifying aspects of their pr
 actice.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTo this\, we welcome a broad range of proposals f
 ocusing on a variety of both practice- and research-oriented topics in E
 SP.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSuggested generalic areas include but are certainly n
 ot limited to: \n\n\n\n·              Pedagogy & practice in ESP  \n\n\n
 \n·                Challenges (andolutions) facing ESP \n\n\n\n·        
         Changing workplace ESP nee & expectations \n\n\n\n·             
    Changing student ESP needs & exctations  \n\n\n\n·                AI 
 & writing in the ESP classroo \n\n\n\n·                The role of EAP i
 n ESP  \n\n\n\n·            ESP\, culture & world Englishes \n\n\n\n  \n
 \n\n\nWe invite you tbmit a proposal for one of the following (Deadline 
 31st October 2023):   \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTalk  \n\n\n\nLength: 30 minutes (
 20 presentationQ&A)  \n\n\n\nPractice- or research-oriented talks are we
 lcome.  \n\n\n\n\nWorkshop \n\n\n\nLength: 60 or 90 minutes \n\n\n\nWork
 shops sbe practical and hands-on.  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPoster \n\n\n\nPresen
 tatigth: 10 minutes \n\n\n\nPractice- or research-oriented posters (size
 : A1)re welcome.  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nGeneral proposal format:  \n\n\n\nYour
 sal will consist of a short abstract (70 words) and a longer summary (25
 0 words) of your talk/workshop/poster\, as well as a short biographical 
 text for each presentation (70 words).  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPlease click her
 e<htt/forms.office.com/Pages/ResponsePage.aspx?id=qElTS75CakWhLe_Sr4BEcg
 pNhVG0gHpKp4PgicfnmwdUQ0w3MTA4SU1LUVozOEtLSzNFSDI1S1dIMSQlQCN0PWcu> to a
 ccess the speaker submission form.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOur event website is a
 ccessible hereps://www.fhwn.ac.at/en/events/common-ground-in-esp>.\n\n\n
 \nBest wishes\,\nlrike Pavelka & Team\n\n\n\nCommon Ground in ESP\n\nIns
 titute of Languages_____________________________________________________
 _______________________\n\n\n\nESP2024@fhwn.ac.at<mailto:ESP2024@fhwn.ac
 .at>\n\n\n\nUniversity oflied Sciences\n\nFachhochschule Wiener Neustadt
  GmbH – Campus 1\n\nJohann Gutenberg-Str. 3 l A-2700 Wiener Neustadt\n\n
 \n\nPerspectives through appld learning – practice-based education in Au
 stria:\n\nWiener Neustadt: Camus 1 l City Campus\n\nWieselburg: Marketin
 g Campus l Campus Francisco Josepinum\n\nTulln: Biotech Campus\n\nVienna
 : Campus Rudolfinerhaus\n\n_____________________________________________
 _____________________________\n\n\n\nfh.ac.at<http://www.fhwn.ac.at/> | 
 facebook.com/fhwnfan<http://www.facebook.com/fhwnfan> | instagram.com/fh
 wienerneustadt<ttps://www.instagram.com/fhwienerneustadt>
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Vienna:20230718T110000
DTSTAMP:20260910T205509Z
