BEGIN:VEVENT
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20220322T132110Z
DESCRIPTION:Dear All\,\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nIt is with great pleasure that I 
 can announce a SSS-patch-in to a talk being\n\nheld by Dr. Maximilian Bu
 rger-Scheidlin – the executive Director of the\n\nInternational Chamber 
 of Commerce Austria - on the subject of ‘Corruption\n\nand its Significa
 nce to the Security of Countries – the Example Of Ukraine\n\n(Amongst Ot
 hers)’. Dr Burger-Scheidlin is a leading expert in the field of\n\ncorru
 ption\, having authored numerous publications – including three books –\
 n\non the impacts of corruption\, the prevention of corruption\, and the
 \n\ndevelopment of business more generally\; as well as having had a car
 eer’s\n\nworth of experience holding anti-corruption seminars\, teaching
  law and\n\nbusiness at university level and acting as an international 
 consultant in\n\nthis sector.  This talk promises to be both stimulating
  and topical\, and\,\n\ngiven Dr. Burger-Scheidlin’s considerable public
  speaking experience\,\n\ncaptivating and engaging. \n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n‘Co
 rruption and its Significance on the Security of Countries – the Example
 \n\nOf Ukraine (Amongst Others)’ will cover the following points:\n\n\n\
 n \n\n\n\n- The impact of corruption on emerging economies\n\n\n\n- Is t
 here a connection between the ongoing wars\, civil unrest and\n\ncorrupt
 ion?\n\n\n\n- Key players in many “difficult” countries are corrupt - ca
 n corruption be\n\nfought?\n\n\n\n- Is the present global legal approach
  to anti-corruption showing tangible\n\nresults? – What might the altern
 atives be?\n\n\n\n- In your own business - how to avoid corruption and s
 till be successful\n\n\n\n- Better practice examples: The Baltic States\
 , Singapore\, Mauritius\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nThe talk will last approximately
  45 minutes and be held in English. Then\,\n\nthere will be approximatel
 y 30 minutes for questions and answers (both\n\nEnglish and German and a
 lso via the zoom chat).\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nThe talk will be held at 19:30 o
 n Friday\, 25 March (this Friday). The talk\n\nwill be held at the FH bu
 t as part of a pre-arranged event (@Martin van Dam\n\nthank you very muc
 h indeed for organising this talk and letting us\n\ngate-crash!). I woul
 d\, therefore\, ask you to join via the zoom patch-in:\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nJ
 oin Zoom Meeting\n\n\n\nhttps://technikum-wien-at.zoom.us/j/96032304001?
 pwd=UlpQVnJteUpNSzBLNGdFQ2hX\n\nQUxnQT09\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nThis informatio
 n can also be found on our SSS Discord server (you can also\n\nuse this 
 link to join SSS):\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nhttps://discord.gg/vRAkHv3wFW\n\n\n\n
  \n\n\n\nI am very much looking forward to seeing some of you then!\n\n\
 n\n \n\n\n\nBest\,\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nDavid\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nMag. D
 avid Warren\n\n\n\nDepartment Entrepreneurship & Communications \n\n\n\n
 Lektor\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nFachhochschule Technikum Wien\n\n\n\nHöchstädtpla
 tz 5\, 1200 Wien\n\n\n\nT: +43 676 50 11 903\n\n\n\nE:  <mailto:david.wa
 rren@technikum-wien.at> david.warren@technikum-wien.at\n\n\n\nI:  <http:
 //www.technikum-wien.at/> www.technikum-wien.at
