 y) at 10am (Irish time) entitled ‘Introduction to Persuasion and Influen
 ce Techniques’.\\r\n\\r\nIn the webinar I will discuss communications sk
 ills and teciques that we can all employ to persuade others\, sway decis
 ions\, negotiate outcomes\, cultivate cooperation\, and sell products or
  ourselves.\\r\n\\rhe webinar is free to attend\, and you can register t
 hrough the link below. Please feel free to forward onto to anyone else w
 ho you think may be interested.\\r\n\\r\nEssential Skills Session 37 - I
 ntroduction to Persuasion and fluence Techniques (engineersireland.ie)<h
 ttps://www.engineersireland.ie/Events/event/9629>\\r\n\\r\nI hope you en
 joy it.\\r\n\\r\nRegards\,\\r\n\\r\n[turn ges]<https://www.tudublin.ie/>
 \\r\nStephen Harper MEng\, CEng\, MIEI\, PG Cet\\r\nAssistant Lecturer\\
 r\nErasmus coordinator\\r\nSchool of Transport and Cl Engineering\\r\nBo
 lton Street\\r\nTechnological University Dublin\\r\n____________________
