BEGIN:VEVENT
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20230717T063606Z
DESCRIPTION:Hi Mark\,\n\n\n\nPoints:\n\n\n\nWritten test 60%\n\nVocal: 1
 0%class discussions: 5 x 6% = 30%\n\n(For these\, I’ll prepare 25 discus
 sio questions for each topic\, together with a simple grading sheet. Tea
 chers can decide how they best want to implement these discussions).\n\n
 \n\nTimin\n\n\n\nI suppose it is possible to have the writing and the vo
 cab in the sce of 80 minutes\, however if the written test and the vocab
  test collectively have 70% of the grade\, then 80 minutes is a little s
 hort for both…. The other problem I have is that it leaves us with nothi
 ng to do at all in the final 2 units as\, unlike in previous semesters\,
  there is no oral presentation to prepare for. What could we use the fin
 al 2 lessons for?\n\n\n\npragmatic solution to this would be: \n\n80 min
 ute written test (2 texts) i computer room\n\n20 minute vocabulary test 
 (45 items) either on laptops (SE).\n\n\n\nFor future planning: we either
  need the computer room both all 4essons\, or students need to bring lap
 tops with safe browser installed. \n	he best solution in the future woul
 d be: 60 minutes: review / discussion\, 20 minutes: vocab\, 90 minutes: 
 written test.\n\n\n\nBut as I said\, pragmically speaking\, we can do a 
 shorter version this year on account of the room allocations.\n\n\n\nSee
  you later\,\n\nPaul\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n> On 16.07.2t 22:09\, Mark Adams <ad
 ams@technikum-wien.at> wrote:\n\n> \n\n> Hi Paul \n> \n\n> Before I forg
 et - some questions.\n\n> \n\n> 1. Did you fix the leh of time for the t
 est and for the vocab test? Can we do the writing in an hour and the voc
 ab in 20 minutes or so\, so that it is all in one 2 hour lesson? Many wi
 ll be late getting into the room etc due to change over. Need to think a
 bout that.\n\n> \n\n> 2. We discussed the points for homework etcWas tha
 t then implemented? Some part of grade continuous\, otherwise they don't
  do it. What came out of that discussion with regard to your planning?\n
 > \n\n> Think there were a few more\, but will get back to you when they
  ome back to me.\n\n> \n\n> \n\n> -- \n\n> Best regards\,\n\n> \n\n> Mar
 k AdM.A. O.D.E.\n\n> Entrepreneurship & Communications\n\n> Kompetenzfel
 dleitunSprachen\n\n> Fachhochschule Technikum Wien\n\n> Höchstädtplatz 6
 \, A-120Wien\n\n> T: +43 (0)1 3334077-823\n\n> E: mark.adams@technikum-w
 ien.at\n\n> www.technikum-wien.at\n\n
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Vienna:20230724T100000
