BEGIN:VEVENT
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20230307T113029Z
DESCRIPTION:Great\, thanks Mark! I'm free next Monday morning after abou
 t 9.45 and free on Tuesday after a dental appointment I have\, so betwee
 n 2 - 5pm.\\r\nLet me know what's good for you!\\r\n\\r\nBest\,\\r\nPatr
 ick\\r\nOn Tue\, March 07\, 2023 11:59 CET\, Mark Adams <adams@technikum
 -wien.at> wrote:\\rn  \\r\nI think this could be very interesting. We wo
 uld need to see wherewe can combine it for a project etc but I would sup
 port it. Maybe we can brainstorm soon. I am away from Thursday til Sunda
 y but next week would be good. Morning morning or any time or Tuesday be
 fore 5 would work for me if you want to come in or zoom.\\r\n On 07.03.2
 3 11:03\, Patrick Loan wrote:Hi Mrk\,\\r\n\\r\nI've been in touch with N
 ina in the Erasmus coordination officebout Erasmus+ staff mobility and t
 he possibility of going to do a teaching exchange for about a week\, as 
 you suggested when we had the staff meeting back in January.  I also got
  in touch with some institutions which have an art & design department t
 o see if they might be interested in collaborating on a visual arts proj
 ect with the technical students at the Technikum.\\r\\r\nSo\, Hogent (an
  institution in Belgium) are interested in doing somethig\, and they wro
 te back to me\, the email from Mr Hendrik Leper (Tutor and coordinator M
 edia Arts\, School of Arts Ghent) is below. Originally\, I emailed Hogen
 t to see if they would be interested in me going to teach there\, and a 
 possible online collaborative project with our students and their studen
 ts. His proposal would entail me going to Hogent to teach/ give lectures
 / workshops to their students and then\, as he mentioned in his email\, 
 they are keen to visit Vienna\, maybe to work on a collaborative project
  with our students - an interdisciplinary project with the potential to 
 have a physical exhibition at the Technikum and at Hogent\, or maybe jus
 t online.  Setting up exhibitions and running art/ education projects li
 ke this is something I've had a lot of experience with in the past.\\r\n
 \\r\nMy next questn is\, how could I go about getting it off the ground\
 , and would it be possible? If you have time\, maybe we could have a cha
 t about it soon - thanks!\\r\n\\r\nAll the best\,\\r\nPatrick\\r\n\\r\n\
 \r\nEmail from Hendrik Leper Tutocoordinator Media Arts\, School of Arts
  Ghent:\\r\n Dear Patrick\,\\r\n\\r\nFke Velghe (in CC) forwarded me you
 r proposal. I am coordinator of the media arts program (Fine Arts) and r
 ead your proposal with interest. \\r\n\\r\nI d't want to do it any disho
 nor but in post-corona times we all long for physical encounters and col
 laboration. For that reason\, I doubt the intent of the project which as
 sumes a distance/online collaboration between students.  But I also read
  in your accompanying email that you are open for discussion. From that 
 perspective\, I would like to present you a counterproposal.\\r\n\\r\nCo
 uld we turn it around so that we visit you? There is a preterm anvague p
 lan to undertake a trip with students to Vienna within the next academic
  year (2023-2024). There is currently a student in 3rd bachelor media ar
 t (through Erasmus +) from Vienna. His mother is head of the Secession a
 nd would like to host and show us around. Perhaps we could link this vis
 it to a joined project?\\r\n\\r\nI understand that this might be quite a
  reversal  your proposal and will not help you further with the Erasmus+
  teacher mobility. To accommodate each other\, we could also consider a 
 plan in 2 phases. A first part with a visit from you to KASK Ghent follo
 wed by a visit from us to at the University of Applied Sciences Techniku
 m Vienna?\\r\n\\r\nIf yowish\, we can certainly talk about this as well 
 (video chat).\\r\nKind regars and have a nice weekend\\r\n\\r\n Hendrik 
 Leper  (he/him)               Tutor and coordinator Media Arts\\r\n\\r\n
 School of Arts Ghenn----------------------------------------------------
 ------------\\r\nThe Roal Academy of Fine Arts and the Royal Conservator
 y together constitute the School of Arts of University College Ghent\\r\
 n---------------------------------------------------------------\\r\nJoz
 ef Kluyskensstraat 2 \, 9000 GhentBelgium\\r\nhttps://schoolofartsgent.b
 e/   https://www.mediakunst.be/-- \\rBest regards\,\\r\n\\r\nMark Adams\
 , M.A. O.D.E.\\r\nEntrepreneurship & Communtions\\r\nKompetenzfeldleitun
 g Sprachen\\r\n\\r\nFachhochschule Technikum WieHöchstädtplatz 6\, A-120
 0 Wien\\r\nT: +43 (0)1 3334077-5178\\r\nE:mark.adamtechnikum-wien.at\\r\
 nI:www.technikum-wien.at\\r\n\\r
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Vienna:20230314T150000
DTSTAMP:20260910T205509Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Vienna:20230314T140000
LAST-MODIFIED:20230308T154941Z
