DESCRIPTION:Dear Paul and Mark\,\n\nPlease see link to webinar below.\n\
 nHo you both have a great Christmas break.\n\n\n\nBest Regards\n\nUna\n\
 n[cid:26ee-08e3-42cd-8958-519246c7feda]\n\n\n\n\n\nDr Una Beagon CEng FI
 StructE M\n\n\n\nHead of Civil Engineering\, School of Transport and Civ
 il Engineeri\n\n\n\n_________________________________\n\n\n\n–  +353 1 2
 20 666 tudublin.ie<https://tudublin.ie/>\n\n\n\nOT Baile Átha Cliath\, S
 ráid lton\, D01 K822\, Éire.\n\n\n\nTU Dublin\, Bolton Street\, D01 K822
 \, Ireld.\n\n\n\nTU Dublin is a registered charity RCN 20204754\n\n[cid:
 e5b9ba32-d-45cb-a497-825e530fa8bf][cid:ce893d4f-c803-4a64-a9ba-7b32f5ac7
 54e]  [cid:7483df2c-a01a-404c-b040-442ea150be46] [cid:ba17fce4-d9cf-4bdd
 -a299-740993b55e90]     [cid:701c3fae-7785-425f-9dea-655907eb4bce] <http
 s://www.tudublin.ie/research/discover-our-research/profess12/about/>\n\n
 \n\nMy latest papers plished in\n\nThe Journal of Engineering Education:
 \n\nUnderstanding professnal skills in engineering education: A phenomen
 ographic study of faculty conceptions<https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/do
 i/full/10.1002/jee.20556>\n\n\nEuropean Journal of Engineering Education
 :\n\nPreparing engineering student for the challenges of the SDGs: what 
 competences are required?<https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/0
 3043797.2022.2033955>\n\n\n\nI would likto support colleagues to have a 
 healthy work/life balance. I’m emailing you now as it works for me.\n\nI
  appreciate that your working arrangements my be different so please res
 pond when convenient for you.\n\n\n\nLinkedIn: a Beagon<https://www.link
 edin.com/in/dr-una-beagon-95566b18/?originalSubdomain=ie>\n\n\n\n\n\n___
 _____________________________\n\nFrom: Máirín Ní Ausa <mairin@engineersi
 reland.ie>\n\nSent: Wednesday 20 December 2023 15:37nSubject: Teaching T
 ransversal Skills to our Engineering Students webinar\nn\n\n\n\n[R.PHOST
  SEACHTRACH] NÁ CLICEÁIL AR naisc nó ceangaltáin ach aáin má aithníonn t
 ú an seoltóir agus go bhfuil a fhios agat gur ábhar sábháilte é\n\n\n\n[
 EXTERNAL EMAIL] DO NOT CLICK links or attachments uess you recognize the
  sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\n\nHi all\nn\n\n\n\nWe trust y
 ou enjoyed our November 30th “Teaching Transversal Skis to our Engineeri
 ng Students” webinar hosted by our Academic society.  The recording is n
 ow published on the Engineers Ireland YouTube channel where it is availa
 ble to view\, and share should you wish.  The link is https://youtu.be/Z
 7cRulao-qc\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOur presenters very kindly agreed to s a pdf v
 ersion of their slide presentations with attendees and copies of these a
 re now attached for you.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nIf you are a member of Engineere
 land\, don’t forget to record your attendance in MyCPD on the website – 
 attending this or any of our sector hosted events can be counted toward 
 your overall CPD target for the year\, as indeed can viewing the recordi
 ngs available to view on Engineers TV on the website.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWe 
 hope ee you at more Engineers Ireland Sector hosted events in the coming
  months – keep an eye on the events page<https://www.engineersireland.ie
 /Events/search?resource=934&resources=935> on our website for more event
 s that might interest you.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWith very best wishes.\n\n\n\n
 \n\n\n\nMáirín Ní Aonghusa | Customer Service Officer | Sector Support |
  Engineers Ireland\, 22 Clyde Road\, Dublin 4 | D04 R3N2 | T: +353 (0)1 
 6651315 | M: +353 (0)87 2405188\n\n\n\n[https://version1-ingature-ei-tes
