DESCRIPTION:Hi Mark\,\n\n\n\nit seems to me that the link to the diversi
 ty worksheet refers directly to the\n\nfile in the quellkurs and is ther
 efore not available for the students.\n\nI re-uploaded the corresponding
  pdf separately and switched the link\, so it's\n\nfixed for the mention
 ed course but the problem still persists in the quellkurs\n\nand the oth
 er semester courses since it is not linked correctly in the\n\nquellkurs
 .\n\n\n\nThere are two options I can suggest to solve it there:\n\n\n\n-
  clearing the link and adding a note in the text that this pdf can be fo
 und\n\nin the folder below\n\n- reupload the worksheet file separately a
 nd switch the link in the text\n\n\n\nSince the students all have access
  to the folder right under the text and the\n\nworksheet there\, I think
  the first option is best for the semester courses and\n\ncan be done by
  the lectureres and the second option is best for fixing it in\n\nthe qu
 ellkurs for the next semesters. Let me know if you need any help with\n\
 nfixing it in the quellkurs or if there are any open questions.\n\n\n\nB
 est regards\n\nSebastian\n\nMoodle Support\n\nTLC - Teaching & Learning 
 Center\n\n\n\n20.02.2022 08:00 - Mark Adams schrieb:\n\n\n\n Hi\n\n\n\n 
 Wahrscheinlich habe ich irgendwie den Link falsch gemacht aber bitte Pro
 blem\n\nunten sehen. Könnt ihr mir sagen was ich faslch gemacht habe?\n\
 n\n\n Vielen Dank.\n\n\n\n-------- Forwarded Message -------- \n\n\n\n S
