DESCRIPTION:Hi Mark\,\\r\n\\r\nHope you're doing well and nearly finishi
 ng uphe semester!\\r\n\\r\nI wonder what you think of the idea to keep t
 he projectelatively low-key\, and I've also been in contact with the guy
  in Gent\, and he wants to keep the project really simple as well. It wo
 uld entail students from the Technikum getting involved voluntarily\, so
  we wouldn't necessarily have to think about Erasmus+ funding for the Te
 chnikum at the moment\, but if it goes well then we could expand it in t
 he future\\r\n\\r\n1. Septeer 2023 -  get students from Technikum involv
 ed (between 6 - 10) - convince students & departments it would be a good
  idea/ benefit them\, and sell it to them!\\r\n2. November 2023 - I woul
 d go to Gent for 2-days to give a seies of F2F workshops (about art\, te
 chnology and collaborative projects)\, and get Technikum students to joi
 n online to propose and outline a potential interdisciplinary collaborat
 ive project with both institutions - if Nov workshops go well\, then mov
 e forward with stage 3.\\r\n3. March 2024 - studets from Gent come on a 
 student visit to Vienna (they were thinking of coming to Vienna on a stu
 dy visit anyway) and work F2F with their Technikum partners - set up sma
 ll exhibition using the space where I have a studio (WEST-space in 9th d
 istrict)\, or a space at the Technikum. Materials for exhibition would n
 eed to be borrowed or provided by the students\, I have some equipment a
 vailable (projector + flat screen TVs etc)\\r\n\\r\nWould really appriat
 e your thoughts on this and if you have any ideas how we could best move
  forward with the project - thanks!\\r\n\\r\nAll the best\,\\r\nPatrick\
 \r\n\\r---- Original Message --------\\r\nSubject: Re: Fwd: AW: Erasmus+
  staff mobiity opportunities to GENT\\r\nDate: Thursday\, June 22\, 2023
  17:00 CEST\\r\nom: Mark Adams <adams@technikum-wien.at>\\r\nTo: Patrick
  Loan <loan@techniku-wien.at>\\r\nReferences: <12ed0b-64921a80-6f-12a4fa
 a0@247160947>\\r\n\\r\n\\r\\r\nHi Patrick\,\\r\nYes this is fine for the
  individual travel and your teaing there which comes under Erasmus mobil
 ity\, but it does not have anything to do with any kind of cooperation o
 n a formal level for a project. This would need to be discussed with the
  international office before you make any kind of plans or promises.\\r\
 n  On 20.06.23 23:31\, Patrick Loan wrote:i Mark\,\\r\n\\r\nThis is the 
 recent (this Monday 19th June) message I got fr Nina in the internationa
 l office.\\r\n\\r\nBest\,\\r\nPatrick\\r\n\\r\n--------inal Message ----
 ----\\r\nSubject: AW: Erasmus+ staff mobility opportunitiesto GENT\\r\nD
 ate: Monday\, June 19\, 2023 14:08 CEST\\r\nFrom: "Nina Thiel" <0055@tec
 hnikum-wien.at>\\r\nTo: "'Patrick Loan'" <loan@technikum-wien.at>\\refer
 ences: <229b1-648f4500-85-3e6d5300@72228039>\\r\n\\r\n\\r\n\\r\n  \\r\nH
 i Pa\,\\r\n\\r\n\\r\n \\r\nSounds good to me. Yes\, September is fine\, 
 still enouime to complete the documents. For the time period you mention
 ed 14-16th of November and 2 travel days the calculated Erasmus+ grant w
 ould be EUR 875\,- (in case you travel green\, you can add another EUR 4
 5\,-). \\r\n\\r\n\\r\nThe grant will be transferred to the faculty after
  having completed the Erasmus+ documents. In case you want to book your 
 transportation and accommodation earlier you can check with Mark what is
  the best way (either via our travel agency\, if the faculty advances mo
 ney or if you pay it yourself and have it reimbursed).\\r\n\\r\n\\r\n \\
 r\nIf you have any more questions\, pl let me know.\\r\n\\r\n\\r\n \\r\n
 Best regards\\r\n\\r\nNina  \\r\n\\r\n--\\r\n\\rdlichen Grüßen/ Kind reg
 ards\\r\n\\r\nMag. Nina Thiel\\r\n\\r\nProject- & Moby Coordinator\, | P
 rojekt- und Mobilitätskoordination\\r\nStaff Mobility | ersonalmobilität
 \\r\nInternational Office | Internationales Büro\\r\n\\r\nFaochschule Te
 chnikum Wien | University of Applied Sciences Technikum Wien\\rHoechstae
 dtplatz 6\, 1200 Wien\, AUSTRIA \\r\n\\r\nT: +43 1 333 40 77-3183\\r +43
  1 333 40 77-99323\\r\nE: nina.thiel@technikum-wien.at\\r\nI: www.techni
 k-wien.at\\r\n\\r\n\\r\n -- \\r\nBest regards\, \\r\n\\r\nMark Adams\, M
 .A. O.D.ntrepreneurship & Communications\\r\nKompetenzfeldleitung Sprach
 en\\r\n \\r\nFhochschule Technikum Wien\\r\nHöchstädtplatz 6\, A-1200 Wi
 en\\r\nT: +43 (0)3334077-823\\r\nE: mark.adams@technikum-wien.at\\r\nI: 
 www.technikum-wien.at 
