DESCRIPTION:Greetings!\n\n\n\nHere are the issues we discussed with Mark
  in last November in Vienna about CIP-project and the English language p
 art. The goal was to support the development of English language and sci
 entific writing\, the students can evolve during the project.\n\n\n\n\n\
 n  1.  English language involved right from the beginning\n\n\n\n     * 
   Presentation of the English language part of the project in the first 
 meeting\n\n\n\n  1.  Comments from the 1st draft of the report (Sanna wo
 uld give the comments)\n\n  2.  In Finland week:\n\n\n\n     *   Present
 ation/guidance how to write the final report\n\n     *   1hr lecture – w
 hat are the most typical mistakes in writing in English etc..\n\n\n\n  1
 .  In Vienna week: Guidance\, how to make and keep a presentation (stude
 nts will give a presentation about the progress in the project)\n\n  2. 
  Comments from the 70% draft of the report (Mark would give the comments
 \, checks 4-5 pages)\n\n\n\nFeel free to add/change\, these were the res
 ults of the brainstorming session in Vienna😊\n\n\n\nBest wishes\,\n\n\n
 \nAri
