DESCRIPTION:> \\r\n> Actually\, already sent Diana the lecturers last we
 ek ad everything has already been entered into the system :-)\\r\n\\r\nG
 reat\, thks!\\r\n\\r\n> \\r\n> For your other question\, caught in the m
 iddle here to bonest.\\r\n> \\r\n> On the one hand we only have 2 semest
 ers of English and t idea was supposed to be that the two semesters woul
 d prepare students for the classes that would come afterwards that were 
 going to be taught in English. If someone is weak and only has 1 semeste
 r of English before those classes\, it makes those classes all the harde
 r.\\r\n\\r\nAs a compromise\, it cld also move it to the 4th semester. T
 hat would at least prepare students for our 5th "international" semester
  which is entirely in English.\\r\n\\r\n>n> On the other hand\, I get th
 e argumentation that it would be financially better as there would be le
 ss groups by the 5th semester due to dropouts.\n> \\r\n> Are you in Tech
 nikum on Wednesday? Maybe we can have coffee and ctch up and chat about 
 it?\\r\n\\r\nSure - maybe in the afternoon?\\r\n\\r\nChee\\r\n\\r\nDavid
 \\r\n\\r\n> \\r\n> \\r\n> On 14.07.23 17:35\, David Meyer wrote:\\r Mark
 \,\\r\n>>\\r\n>> Hope you are not struggling to much with finding additi
 al lecturers for us - crazy times ...\\r\n>>\\r\n>> Would you mind if Bu
 sinesEnglish was moved from the current 2nd Sem. to the 5th? It would me
 an that BE will not take place in Summer 24 and Summer 25\, and start ag
 ain in Winter 25/26\, with less groups than in the 2nd semester (I guess
 \, 4 in the Tagesform and 3 in the Abendform).\\r\n>>\\r\n>> Cheers\,\\r
 \n>>\\r\n>> Davi
