BEGIN:VEVENT
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20221215T142554Z
DESCRIPTION:Dear all\,\n\n\n\nI’m attaching an up-to-date summary of pre
 linary ideas\, activities and partnerships for the proposed project ECO-
 GT (Young Engineers Communicating and Collaborating for the Green Transi
 tion). I have checked the deadline again\, and now it seems they’ve brou
 ght it forward to 22. March (it was 10. April for a while) - although I 
 am confident of having a solid proposal in place by mid March either way
 .\n\n\n\nOur nt steps would be:\n\n\n\na) Get an idea of any reliable ex
 isting partnershi across the 7 partners countries I identified (see docu
 ment attached - I’ve tried to maintain a geographic balance as well as a
  balance of ‘expensive’ and ‘low cost’ countries\; Poland is a great app
 licant country\, Ireland is necessary - without having a country with En
 glish as an official language\, the reviewer might not accept any Englis
 h language focus - this happened to me before!\; Mark said he’d already 
 garnered interest in Sweden?) Ideally then I would like contact the inst
 itutions individually to discuss their interest / ideas and how they cou
 ld contribute.\n\n \n\nb) Wita clear idea of the partnership organisatio
 ns and their specific contributions\, I can circulate a draft budget and
  work plan for agreement. This ideally needs to be in place by mid to la
 te January.\n\n\n\nOther than that\,’ll keep populating the preparation 
 template document\, although I won’t be able to access the correct appli
 cation form until it is published on 10th January. For this\, I would al
 so need access to Technikum Wien’s ECAS application portal.\n\n\n\nI wou
 ld be free to meet either next Monday (19t anytime in the morning\; othe
 rwise I’m available again on the 2nd and 3rd January.\n\n\n\nSpeak soon.
 \n\n\n\nBest\,\n
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Vienna:20221219T110000
DTSTAMP:20260910T205509Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Vienna:20221219T100000
LAST-MODIFIED:20221215T142620Z
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Erasmus+ Cooperation Partnership Project - Update
