 QKmuDUgGC4_zSg\n	Description: With the 'roar' of generative AI\, we are 
 seeing a paradigm shift in teaching\, learning and assessment. \nIn the 
 context of higher education there is increasing demand for students to p
 repare for real-world application of skills\, such as problem solving\, 
 critical thinking and communication.\n\nSo what specific communicative E
 nglish skills do international students need to survive and thrive in su
 ch rapidly evolving academic settings?\nJoin our webinar where we will d
 iscuss our views on this and share how students can develop these skills
  through English tests like LanguageCert Academic.\n\nThe session will i
 nclude:\n· practical examples of specific skills embedded in the Languag
 eCert Academic test\n· a look at some of the task types in the test and 
 how we approach integration of skills\n· an update on our ongoing resear
 ch program\n· time for your questions and comments.\n\nRegister today to
  secure your place.\n\n
