 Temat: Publication of your project: 2023-1-PL01-KA220-HED-000165199\n\n\
 n\nRef. Project: 2023-1-PL01-KA220-HED-000165199 - Notification of proje
 ct publication\n\nDear Maciej Sawicki\,\n\nWe kindly inform you that for
  ensuring transparency and visibility of EU funding\, your project "Engi
 neers Communicating and Collaborating Internationally for the Green Tran
 sition" is now online on the Erasmus+ Project Results Platform<https://e
 rasmus-plus.ec.europa.eu/projects/search/>.\n\nA description of your pro
 ject\, where applicable\, has been published online at the following add
 ress: Project Card<https://erasmus-plus.ec.europa.eu/projects/search/det
 ails/2023-1-PL01-KA220-HED-000165199>\n\nYou can start uploading on the 
 Erasmus+ Project Results Platform<https://erasmus-plus.ec.europa.eu/proj
 ects/search/> additional information (website\, logo\, project results) 
 about your project in the Beneficiary's dashboard<https://webgate.ec.eur
 opa.eu/education_culture/dissemination/share> or the new platform Erasmu
 s+ and European Solidarity Corps Projects (EESCP*)<https://webgate.ec.eu
 ropa.eu/erasmus-esc/index/>. To access the results section\, please clic
 k on the search results and scroll down to display the results section. 
 This helpdesk does not handle technical questions related to the EESCP\,
  please refer to the EESCP support section.\n\nYou are encouraged to mak
 e the project website visible on the platform as soon as it is available
 \, as it enhances the project's visibility.\n\nYou can connect using you
 r EU Login account.\n\nEnsure that your EU Login account is associated t
 o msawicki@pg.edu.pl e-mail address.\n\nIf you do not have an EU Login a
 ccount associated to the above mentioned e-mail address\, you can create
  one following the instructions available on the EU Login page<https://w
 ebgate.ec.europa.eu/cas/eim/external/help.cgi>.\n\nYou can also manage t
 he contact details of your organisation and of your project partners - w
 hich are currently hidden by default. Displaying the contacts details wi
 ll add visibility to your project\, your organisation and your project p
 artners\, helping other interested organisations to contact you for coop
 eration and/or future projects.\n\nYou should keep in mind that you will
  be able to submit your project results (i.e. outputs) for review by you
 r project officer and publication only when the end date of your project
  has been reached. In the meantime\, you can upload and modify your proj
 ect results\, but they will become publicly available only after the val
 idation of your final report.\n\n\nKind regards\,\n\nThe Erasmus+ Projec
 t Results Platform\n\nThe Erasmus+ and European Solidarity Corps platfor
 m (EESCP) is the single entry point to the Erasmus+ and European Solidar
 ity Corps programmes for the Multiannual Financial Framework 2021-2027. 
 It enables applicants and beneficiaries to:\n\n\n  *   Search for regist
 ered organisations participating in Erasmus+ or European Solidarity Corp
 s decentralised actions\,\n  *   Register their organisation for partici
 pation in Erasmus+ or European Solidarity Corps decentralised actions\,\
 n  *   Submit applications for grants and/or accreditation for decentral
 ised actions\,\n  *   And manage ongoing projects\n\nThe page is accessi
 ble even if you do not yet have an EU Login account\, however most of th
 e actions you can perform as an applicant or awarded beneficiary require
  signing in. Applicants/Beneficiaries/Experts can find more information 
 available in Erasmus+ and European Solidarity Corps guides<https://wikis
 .ec.europa.eu/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=33530769>.\n\n\nThis is an au
 tomatic email. Please do not reply to this email\, unless your question 
 is about a technical problem with the Project Results Platform. In case 
 you have questions for the project officer at the National Agency / Exec
 utive Agency\, we advise you to send your reply directly to the project 
 officer.\n\n\nPrivacy: Your data is processed in accordance with Regulat
 ion (EU) 2021/817 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 20 Ma
 y 2021 establishing Erasmus+: the Union Programme for education and trai
 ning\, youth and sport and repealing Regulation (EU) No 1288/2013\; Regu
 lation (EU) 2021/818 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 20
  May 2021 establishing the Creative Europe Programme (2021 to 2027) and 
 repealing Regulation (EU) No 1295/2013\; and Regulation (EU) 2021/888 of
  the European Parliament and of the Council of 20 May 2021 establishing 
 the European Solidarity Corps Programme and repealing Regulations (EU) 2
 018/1475 and (EU) No 375/2014. In line with our privacy statement\, your
  contact data may be published for a maximum of ten years after the end 
 of the programme.\n\n\nGdansk University of Technology\nFaculty of Civil
  and Environmental Engineering\nProject Office\nul. Narutowicza 11/12\n8
 0-233 Gdańsk\, Poland\nwww.pg.edu.pl<http://www.pg.edu.pl>\ntel. +485834
 72764\n19.01.2024 08:28 Maciej Sawicki <maciej.sawicki@pg.edu.pl> napisa
 ł(a):\n\n\nDear All\,\nCould you please hold on with signing the agreeme
