 4 16:06 Paul Talbot <talbot@technikum-wien.at> napisał(a):\n\n\n\nDear M
 aciej\, Dear All\,\n\n\nAfter reviewing the contract\, our legal departm
 ent note that almost none of their concerns have been accepted.\n\n\nMos
 t importantly: Technikum is not even listed among the partners who are s
 upposed to sign the contract – see for example Article 8.\n\n\nThe follo
 wing is still missing:\n\no   Regulations for publications and the use o
 f results in teaching\n\no   severability clause\n\no   regulations for 
 decision-making within the consortium\n\no   Appropriate wording for the
 se can be found for example in the DESCA model contract. See https://www
 .desca-agreement.eu/fileadmin/user_upload/03_ueber_uns/organisation/Inte
 rnationale_Bueros/Bruessel/DESCA/20221118_DESCA_HorizonEurope_Version_1.
 1_elucidations_PDF_final.pdf Sections 8.4.2 (publications) 11.1 (severab
 ility) and 6 (governance structure). The FFG model consortium agreement 
 could also serve as a template: https://www.ffg.at/sites/default/files/d
 ownloads/Musterkonsortialvertrag_Englisch.pdf (Articles 15\, 25.1 and 10
 ). Liability regulations can be found in the DESCA Model Agreement under
  Article 5 and in the FFG model consortium agreement under Article 19.\n
 \no   The numbering of the articles is still incorrect (there are 2 Arti
 cle 12s)\n\no   Applicable law: We accept Polish law provided it does no
 t concern documentation and retention obligations. Regarding the documen
 tation of expenses and the retention of receipts the regulations of the 
 nation-states where the consortium partners are located should apply. Th
 erefore Austrian law would apply to us in these matters. This is not rec
 orded in the contract.\n\no   In the Partnership Agreement under "Paymen
 t arrangements" (Article 5) a precise payment schedule should be include
 d.\n\no   The Partnership Agreement includes a clause on OER (Article 11
 .4.2). The licenses to be used are not specified.\n\n\nPlease could thes
 e issues be addressed ASAP!\n\n\nBest\,\n\nPaul\n\n\n\n\n\nPaul Talbot\,
