BEGIN:VEVENT
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20250123T113117Z
DESCRIPTION:Dear Mr. Adams\,\n \nI am writing regarding your appointment
  suggestion. Tomorrow\, I have both class and a semester graduation even
 t in the afternoon. Would it be possible to reschedule our meeting to Fr
 iday\, or is Thursday the last feasible date? I deeply appreciate the op
 pertunity you have already offered me\, and I apologize for any inconven
 ience this request may cause. If rescheduling to Friday is not an option
 \, I will do my best to accommodate the original arrangement tomorrow an
 d will follow up with an email to confirm a suitable time.\nThank you ve
 ry much for your understanding and support.\n \nKind regards\,\n\nSebast
 ian Füllenhals\n\nAm Mittwoch\, Januar 22\, 2025 18:09 CET\, schrieb Mar
 k Adams <adams@technikum-wien.at>:\n\n \nHi Sebastian\, \n \nI can offer
  you tomrrow (Thursday) either at 4pm or at 4:30pm. \n \nPlease let me k
 now. \n \n\n On 22.01.25 15:21\, Sebastian Fuellenhals wrote:\n \nDear M
 r. Adams\,\n \nI hope this message finds you well.\nI am writing to kind
 ly inquire if there might be an alternative opportunity or date to discu
 ss my English paper with you. Unfortunately\, I missed the chance to boo
 k an appointment\, and it seems that all available slots are now taken.\
 nIf possible\, I would greatly appreciate it if you could provide me wit
 h another date to review and discuss my paper. Your support in this matt
 er would mean a lot to me.\nThank you very much for your understanding a
 nd consideration.\nI look forward to your response.\n \nKind regards\,\n
 \nSebastian Füllenhals\n\n\n\n 
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Vienna:20250128T130000
DTSTAMP:20260910T205509Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Vienna:20250128T123000
LAST-MODIFIED:20250124T191931Z
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Masterthesis Correction
TRANSP:OPAQUE
UID:ef3c7de6-1a82-42e3-b20a-a04555f3815d
URL;VALUE=URI:mid:3de35a-67917200-11-69a7c600@184099837
X-MOZ-GENERATION:2
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20250123T185627Z
DESCRIPTION:Liebe Kolleg:innen (English version below)\,\n\n \n\nalle Mi
 tarbeiter:innen der FH Technikum Wien sind herzlich eingeladen\, an\nden
  folgenden Internationalization at Home Aktivitäten\, organisiert seiten
 s\nInternational Office\, im Sommersemester 2025 teilzunehmen:\n\n \n\n*
 	Für Mitarbeiter:innen wird ein Webinar zum Thema Personalmobilität\n(St
 aff mobility for teaching and/or training) im außer-europäischen Raum\no
 rganisiert\, die aus übrigen Erasmus+ Mitteln in die folgenden Regionen 
 zur\nVerfügung steht: Argentinien\, Mongolei\, Mexiko\, Südafrika\, USA.
  Die\nVeranstaltung findet am Mittwoch\, 26. Februar von 15.00 bis 16.00
  Uhr statt.\nEine separate Aussendung inkl. Anmeldeinformation folgt. \n
 \n \n\n*       Scandinavian Breakfast: Der nächste Thementag steht ganz 
 im Zeichen\nvon Skandinavien. Wir starten den Tag gemeinsam mit Kaffee u
 nd Zimtschnecken\nund lernen dabei unsere Partnerhochschulen in Dänemark
 \, Finnland und\nSchweden kennen. Wir freuen uns auf Euren/ Ihren Besuch
  am Dienstag\, 11.\nMärz um 10.00 Uhr (Raum: Aula Gebäude A).\n\n \n\n*	
 Der (Inter)National Co-Worker Lunch bietet (inter)nationalen\nKolleg:inn
 en die Möglichkeit\, in einer informellen Atmosphäre Kontakte zu\nknüpfe
 n. Für Mittagessen wird gesorgt. Join us: Mittwoch\, 19. März von 12.30\
 nbis 14.00 Uhr (Raum: Social Space im International Office\, B6.05).  \n
 \n \n\n*	Wie jedes Jahr werden wir einen Besuch zu unseren Partnerhochsc
 hulen\nin einem Nachbarland organisieren. Der nächste Tag wird im Sommer
 semester\norganisiert\, wir besuchen die Brno University of Technology (
 \n<https://www.vut.cz/en/> https://www.vut.cz/en/) inkl. Stadtführung am
 \nFreitag\, 28. März 2025. Eine separate Aussendung inkl. Anmeldeinforma
 tion\nfolgt. \n\n \n\n*	Thematische Spaziergänge durch die Stadt Wien: E
 ugene Quinn wird\nsich im Zuge unserer International Week zum Thema Thir
 d Mission und\nCommunity Outreach der Brigittenau widmen. Geplanter Tite
 l: Exploring\nBrigittenau: A Community Walk Through History\, Culture\, 
 and Modern Life in\nVienna’s 20th district. Am: Dienstag\, 13. Mai von 1
 2.00 bis 14.00 Uhr\,\nTreffpunkt: Höchstädtplatz\, vor der FH.\n\n \n\n*
        Workshop on Internationalization for all staff members: Um alle\n
 Hochschulangehörigen zu unterstützen\, die internationalen Vorhaben der 
 FH\nTechnikum Wien so gut es geht umzusetzen\, bietet das International 
 Office\neinen Workshop rund um das Thema Internationalisation@Home. Im R
 ahmen des\nWorkshops wird deutlich\, welche Strategie die FH Technikum W
 ien verfolgt und\nwie jede:r einzelne einen Beitrag leisten und von inte
 rkulturellem Austausch\nprofitieren kann. Save the date: Dienstag\, 24. 
 Juni\, 9.00 bis 12.00 Uhr\n(Anmeldung über Moodle Interne Weiterbildung)
 .\n\n \n\nDas International Office freut sich auf zahlreiche Teilnahme!\
 n\n\n\nCountry-themed evenings on our campus: United States\, October 20
 24. \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\nDear colleagues\,\n\n \n\nAll staff members of UA
 S Technikum Wien are invited to participate in the\nfollowing Internatio
 nalization at Home activities organized by the\nInternational Office in 
 the summer semester 2025:\n\n \n\n*	A webinar will be organised on the t
 opic of staff mobility for\nteaching and/or training outside Europe\, wh
 ich is possible from available\nErasmus+ funds in the following regions:
  Argentina\, Mongolia\, Mexico\, South\nAfrica\, USA. The event will tak
 e place on Wednesday\, 26 February from 15:00\nto 16:00. A separate e-ma
 il including webinar link will follow. \n\n \n\n*	Scandinavian Breakfast
 : The country-specific morning is all about\nScandinavia. We will start 
 the day together with coffee and cinnamon buns\nand get to know our part
 ner universities in Denmark\, Finland\, and Sweden. We\nlook forward to 
 starting the day with you on Tuesday\, 11 March at 10.00\n(Room: Aula Bu
 ilding A).\n\n \n\n*	The (Inter)National Co-Worker Lunch offers (inter)n
 ational\ncolleagues the opportunity to socialize in an informal atmosphe
 re. Lunch\nwill be provided. Join us on Wednesday\, 19 March from 12.30 
 to 14.00 (Room:\nSocial Space in the International Office\, B6.05).  \n\
 n \n\n*	As every year\, we will organise a visit to our partner universi
 ties\nin a neighbouring country. The next day will be organised in the s
 ummer\nsemester\, we will visit the Brno University of Technology\n(http
 s://www.vut.cz/en/) including a city tour on Friday\, 28 March 2025. A\n
 separate e-mail including registration information will follow. \n\n \n\
 n*	Thematic walks through the city of Vienna: Eugene Quinn will be\nfocu
 ssing on Brigittenau as part of our International Week on third mission\
 nand community engagement. Tentative title: Exploring Brigittenau\, A\nC
 ommunity Walk Through History\, Culture\, and Modern Life in Vienna's 20
 th\ndistrict. On: Tuesday\, 13 May from 12.00 to 14.00\, meeting point:\
 nHöchstädtplatz\, in front of FH.\n\n \n\n*	Workshop on Internationalisa
 tion for all staff members: In order to\nsupport all university members 
 in implementing the international projects of\nUAS Technikum Wien as wel
 l as possible\, the International Office offers a\nworkshop on the topic
  of Internationalisation@Home. The workshop will\nexplain the strategy p
 ursued by UAS Technikum Wien and how each individual\ncan make a contrib
 ution and benefit from intercultural exchange. Save the\ndate: Tuesday\,
  24 June\, 9.00 to 12.00 (registration from February via Moodle\nInterna
 l Continuing Education).\n\n \n\nThe International Office is looking for
 ward to many participants!
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Vienna:20250319T140000
DTSTAMP:20260910T205509Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Vienna:20250319T123000
LAST-MODIFIED:20250123T185706Z
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:International Lunch 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
UID:d01f73c9-9dda-4f0b-b539-b9901051866c
URL;VALUE=URI:mid:05d901db6b4f$0ed685d0$2c839170$@technikum-wien.at
END:VEVENT
