DESCRIPTION:Hi both\,\n\nI’ve reworked the flowchart instructions for 2n
 d/Panel exam attempts. This new version includes:\n\n<75% = not eligible
  for 1st attempt at all and goes straight to 2nd attempt appointment (be
 cause the 2nd attempt will now\, as a ‘whole exam’ also include content 
 questions)\n2nd attempts and panel exams are\, in principle\, organised 
 centrally\n\nMy preference is that both 2nd attempt and panel exams (at 
 least for Technical English) are 4 unit exams. This means that students 
 have 2 units for the written texts and then 2 units during which we can 
 test them more rigorously on course/self-study content. How this transla
 tes to the Business English course will depend on whether David wants to
  keep the 100% presentation assessment or not—which I think may need to 
 be up for discussion when we meet in May to review the course.\n\nFor th
 is to function effectively\, as discussed with Mark\, we need the follow
 ing system in place by next semester:\n\nEach internal lecturer is respo
 nsible as LV-lead for X number of study programmes\nLV lead maintains a 
 spreadsheet of all students in their respective purview and is responsib
 le for liaising with individual lecturers for clarity on attendance\, po
 sitive/negative grades\n3 weeks after the last set of exams\, we have a 
 team meeting to clearly identify which students need what moving forward
  and allow us to act immediately.\n\nThis approach will help us maintain
  the necessary overview and prevent the massive headaches from the last 
 semester of not knowing who needs what\, when\, and with whom.\n\nDo we 
 need anything else to be clarified in this process before we finalise it
 ?\n\nBest\,\nPaul\n\n\n\n\n￼
